    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that, but \"precious gift\" feels like such a stretch when you look at the actual math. if it's all just destined to dissolve, then the struggle itself is just adding more noise to a system that's already decaying. it feels like we're just fighting a losing battle against physics. if the end state is always zero, isn't it more \"logical\" to just accept the entropy early rather than exhausting yourself trying to hold onto something that isn't even real in the long run?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
